---
// Two-up module: agent handoffs + local-first privacy.
---
<section style="padding:8px 0 96px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="divide-grid mtypes-2 reveal" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">
      <div class="cell" style="padding:44px 40px">
        <span class="eyebrow mono">Handoffs</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-top:14px;font-weight:500">Move work between agents without losing intent.</h3>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px;max-width:40ch">
          Set a stage, watch until it changes, and let the next local agent pick up the plan, evidence, and blockers another agent left behind.
        </p>
        <div class="mono" style="margin-top:20px;font-size:13px;color:var(--faint)">
          <div><span class="c-blue">$</span> zenith stage set review</div>
          <div><span class="c-blue">$</span> zenith watch --until review.done</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell" style="padding:44px 40px">
        <span class="eyebrow mono">Local-first</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-top:14px;font-weight:500">Private by default. No cloud.</h3>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px;max-width:40ch">
          Guidance context lives in a single SQLite file at <span class="mono c-fg">~/.zenith/zenith.db</span>. No account, no API key, no telemetry leaving your laptop. Your project context stays yours.
        </p>
        <div style="margin-top:20px;display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <span class="pill mono">no external API</span>
          <span class="pill mono">MIT licensed</span>
          <span class="pill mono">Bun + TypeScript</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
